If you are reading this - this INSTALL covers the native systems (defined in ./COMPAT)

GNU+Linux/UNIX-like/HaikuOS:
	Install SDL1.2 library across your device with a package manager.
	Linux (Ubuntu):
		sudo apt install libsdl1.2-dev
	HaikuOS:
		pkgman install libsdl
	Install make and gcc (Should be preinstalled)
	Run 'make'
	The executable will be called 'Pong.out'

Windows:
From Linux:
	Install make and i686-w64-mingw32-gcc
	Ubuntu/Debian:
		sudo apt install mingw-w64-i686-dev 
	Run 'make win_9x_DOS'
	The executable will be called 'Pong_w95_i386.exe'
From Windows:
	Install Visual Studio (Tested on VS 2013)
	Open this as visual studio project (ConsoleApplication1.vcxproj)
	Click Build > Build ConsoleApplication1
	It should make a executable called "Pong.exe"

!!! Idk how to do things on windows so when you compile from Windows make sure the exe is in the same folder as SDL.dll
(SDL-Windows/SDL*/lib/x86/SDL.dll <- It's here) 
